sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor T as Order drafter / data filler (in a hearing)
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant OR as Backend (orders)
    participant AP as Backend (applications)

    Note over T,AP: Screen: hearing order (order-door-screen), Applications section under the items (APL-01)
    T->>FE: Open the hearing's order
    FE->>OR: POST /orders/ {hearing_id} (returns the live order if one exists) or GET /orders/{id}/
    OR-->>FE: 200 order {id, case, hearing, items, data_version}
    FE->>AP: GET /cases/{case_id}/applications/?pending=true
    AP-->>FE: 200 [PENDING_REVIEW or PENDING_DECISION rows with onboarded, decision_date, objections_invited]
    FE-->>T: Applications pending on the matter, each with its type, number and where it stands

    opt Read one before deciding
        T->>FE: Open application
        FE->>AP: GET /applications/{id}/
        AP-->>FE: 200 detail with document
    end

    T->>FE: Answer the application in this order (onboard, defer, dismiss, decide or move date)
    FE->>OR: POST /orders/{id}/items/ If-Match d-n<br/>{item_type: APPLICATION_ACTION, target_id: application_id, values}
    alt Added
        OR-->>FE: 201 item {problems}
    else The application already has an item on this order
        OR-->>FE: 409 E11009 (combination rule 4: one per application per order)
    else Not open (draft, decided, expired)
        OR-->>FE: 409 E11008 APPLICATION_NOT_OPEN
    end

    Note over T,AP: The hearing order is signed and completed like any order. On trigger,<br/>handler.execute runs once per APPLICATION_ACTION item, as in the review and decide diagrams.<br/>The review or decide task closes only if this order acts on the application (ALC-18, ALC-32).
    Note over FE,AP: GAP: listing-applications.ts is demo data and Allowed or Dismissed only writes a sentence into the order.<br/>Replace it with the pending list above and the APPLICATION_ACTION item.
